This product is compatible with, but is not affiliated with or endorsed by,
the Open Source Robotics Foundation or the Open-RMF project. The fleet
adapter architecture follows the patterns documented by the upstream
open-rmf/rmf_ros2 project (rmf_fleet_adapter); the implementation here is
original and does not bundle upstream sources.

The Bazel build for this project fetches the following upstream sources at
build time via `http_archive` and consumes them as deps:

  - open-rmf/rmf_internal_msgs        (release-jazzy-240617)
  - open-rmf/rmf_api_msgs             (release-jazzy-240617)
  - open-rmf/rmf_building_map_msgs    (release-jazzy-240617)
  - open-rmf/rmf_utils                (release-jazzy-240617)
  - open-rmf/rmf_battery              (release-jazzy-240617)
  - open-rmf/rmf_task                 (release-jazzy-240617)
  - open-rmf/rmf_traffic              (release-jazzy-240617, vendored FCL 0.6)
  - open-rmf/rmf_ros2                 (release-jazzy-240617)
  - ros2/domain_bridge
  - ros/pluginlib, ros/class_loader
  - eclipse-zenoh/zenoh-c, eclipse-zenoh/zenoh-cpp

Patches applied to these sources at build time are recorded under
extensions/ in this repository and the patched files are not redistributed
in source form here.
